# Added by cargo

/target

# --- db-gateway repo ignores (kept below the managed block) ---
# Cargo artifacts live outside the guard-recognized target/ directory.
# Every build directory under .cargo/ is ignored, not just target/: an
# audit run may build into .cargo/target-audit/, and a build directory
# that is tracked is a repository that carries its own build output.
/.cargo/target/
/.cargo/target*/
# Session exhaust, never project source.
#
# The managed block above un-ignores these names (!pi-session-*.html,
# !conversation-*.html, !rollout-*.json, !trajectory-*.html) because it
# manages one house style across every repo on this box. For a repo that
# is published, that un-ignore is a leak path and not a style: these are
# decoded transcripts of a working session -- verbatim prompts, tool
# output, file paths, and whatever the operator had on screen. One
# tracked session log (the .md twin of a file the 2026-09-21 audit had
# already untracked) shipped this operator's email address and home
# directory path to every clone. The rules below come after the managed
# block, so they win, and they cover every format rather than the one
# extension a previous audit happened to notice.
pi-session-*
conversation-*
rollout-*
trajectory-*
# Credential material: key files and env files must never be committed.
*.key
.env*
*.pem
# age secrets. The managed block un-ignores .dracon/data/ so the owner
# PUBLIC key can be tracked, and that re-includes everything else under
# it: an encrypted age private key (.age) or a plaintext age identity
# (.agekey) dropped in .dracon/data/keys/ was committable, and a
# committable private key is a published private key.
*.age
*.agekey
